  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.12",
   "range": "MRK.11.12",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "4f8d6c22",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.12#p1-4f8d6c22",
     "text": "This, and that he knew not but that there were figs on the tree, declare him to be the true man.",
     "anchor": "He was hungry"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.13",
   "range": "MRK.11.13",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "93921fb9",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.13#p1-93921fb9",
     "text": "Ver. 13, The time of figs was not yet] viz. Of ripe figs; but if he could have found but green figs only, he would at that time have been glad of them. He looked for somewhat from that great show of leaves. But the old proverb became true, Great bruit, (noise) little fruit."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.14",
   "range": "MRK.11.14",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e09114f6",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.14#p1-e09114f6",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Mat 21:19\"}",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 21:19",
       "ref": "MAT.21.19"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.15",
   "range": "MRK.11.15",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "b8818310",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.15#p1-b8818310",
     "text": "As he had done before, Joh 2:15. {See Trapp on \"Joh 2:15\"} Hath not the Lord done the like also lately among us, casting out many church choppers, that have been money changers rather than ministers in the temple?",
     "anchor": "Began to cast out",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Joh 2:15",
       "ref": "JHN.2.15"
      },
      {
       "text": "Joh 2:15",
       "ref": "JHN.2.15"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.16",
   "range": "MRK.11.16",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "77026352",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.16#p1-77026352",
     "text": "This is one of those things recorded by St Mark only.",
     "anchor": "And would not suffer"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.17",
   "range": "MRK.11.17",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "bd488886",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.17#p1-bd488886",
     "text": "He inveighs against the same fault with the same arguments as before, Joh 2:16-17.",
     "anchor": "My house shall be called, &c.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Joh 2:16-17",
       "ref": "JHN.2.16-17"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.18",
   "range": "MRK.11.18",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "c711dc5b",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.18#p1-c711dc5b",
     "text": "While they hung upon his holy lips, Luk 19:48.",
     "anchor": "Astonished at his doctrine",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Luk 19:48",
       "ref": "LUK.19.48"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.19",
   "range": "MRK.11.19",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "cc950dc9",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.19#p1-cc950dc9",
     "text": "Having first cried, and said, \"He that believeth on me,\" &c., Joh 12:42, to the end of that chapter.",
     "anchor": "He went out of the city",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Joh 12:42",
       "ref": "JHN.12.42"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.20",
   "range": "MRK.11.20",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "4b6dfa8b",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.20#p1-4b6dfa8b",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Mat 21:20\"} Learn to stand in fear of Christ’s curse: he can blow men to destruction, smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, Isa 11:4; Job 4:9.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 21:20",
       "ref": "MAT.21.20"
      },
      {
       "text": "Isa 11:4",
       "ref": "ISA.11.4"
      },
      {
       "text": "Job 4:9",
       "ref": "JOB.4.9"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.21",
   "range": "MRK.11.21",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "bc5cca92",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.21#p1-bc5cca92",
     "text": "So the fig tree bare far better fruit now that it was dried, than when it was green and flourishing. Instruunt nos Patres, tum docentes, tum labentes; The saints teach us, as by their instructions, so by their infirmities. (Aug.)",
     "anchor": "And Peter calling to remembrance"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.22",
   "range": "MRK.11.22",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6d3accde",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.22#p1-6d3accde",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Mat 21:21\"}",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 21:21",
       "ref": "MAT.21.21"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.23",
   "range": "MRK.11.23",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6d3accde",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.23#p1-6d3accde",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Mat 21:21\"}",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 21:21",
       "ref": "MAT.21.21"
      }
