    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.24",
   "range": "MRK.11.24",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "d1c6a786",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.24#p1-5fde2aed",
     "text": "To an effectual prayer two things are here required: 1. An earnest desire after the thing prayed for; \"the desire of the righteous shall be satisfied,\" Pro 10:24; but a cold suitor begs a denial. 2. A confident expectation of a gracious answer. He that prayeth and doubteth shutteth heaven’s gates against his own prayers, Jas 1:7.",
     "anchor": "What things soever ye desire, &c.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Pro 10:24",
       "ref": "PRO.10.24"
      },
      {
       "text": "Jas 1:7",
       "ref": "JAS.1.7"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.24#p2-1401455f",
     "text": "Even as soon as you ask, as the word λαμβαντετ signifies. See Dan 9:20-21; Dan 9:24.",
     "anchor": "Believe that ye receive them",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Dan 9:20-21",
       "ref": "DAN.9.20-21"
      },
      {
       "text": "Dan 9:24",
       "ref": "DAN.9.24"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.25",
   "range": "MRK.11.25",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "fad88f33",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.25#p1-fad88f33",
     "text": "Several gestures in prayer are described, not prescribed, in God’s book. The word στηκητε, here rendered stand, importeth a presenting one’s self before the Lord, whether he stand, sit, or kneel, &c.",
     "anchor": "And when ye stand, praying"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/MRK.11.26",
   "range": "MRK.11.26",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "f9a2a015",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/MRK.11.26#p1-f9a2a015",
     "text": "See Mat 6:14. {See Trapp on \"Mat 6:14\"}",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 6:14",
       "ref": "MAT.6.14"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mat 6:14",
       "ref": "MAT.6.14"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
